{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And you</b> — Yefet said: Migdal David. But the correct interpretation: Jerusalem, for it is like a tower (מגדל) to the flock, which is Israel." "<b>Ophel</b> — like עֹפֶל וּבַחַן (Isaiah 32:14). Some say it is like it in וַיַּעְפִּילוּ (Numbers 14:44), 'they went up to a high ophel'; and thus it is written: לַעֲלֹת אֶל רֹאשׁ הָהָר (Deuteronomy 1:28) — they exalted themselves to go up." "<b>עָדֶיךָ תָּאתֶה</b> — and this word is joined with וּבָאָה. And the meaning: the rulership. And like it: כָּלּוּ תְּפִלּוֹת דָּוִד בֶּן־יִשָׁי (Psalm 72:20), for even though the word תְּפִלּוֹת has an etnaḥ, it is joined to the word דָּוִד; and so is this."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:14:03.748200609Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}